<p>The US military says it destroyed at least 16 Iranian mine-laying vessels near the Strait of Hormuz, and Washington is warning Tehran against placing explosives in the narrow waterway that normally carries about a fifth of the world’s oil and liquefied natural gas. Several outlets also cited US intelligence assessments that say Iran has started, or is preparing, to deploy mines in the strait—raising fears of disruptions to global energy flows. President Trump warned Iran that interference with shipping would draw a stronger US response, as US operations around Hormuz broadened amid what multiple reports described as intensified strikes in the wider US-Israel conflict with Iran. Iran, meanwhile, threatened to block regional oil exports, adding to uncertainty for shipping and energy markets even as oil prices swung on mixed signals from US officials.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/9YYsnZUy6qZUg0oCRmio17T5Oicx-TvP0JqKy5ew_5qJ-PyzvClIEvQJtgIOZbcMt1gYCunACxeQgyGHPwNS6rvdtam2yWdBuG2LphvTzAfOdbqnRqjFGrCIdiE1HOItxBqkEmSJO6p2QTQqfkSm5iGtwYlqt0-GyrH3FlilSgnoDHMZpzuTlWoNnBUDl-VRX_prhvf_' alt='US Central Command-released image related to operations near the Strait of Hormuz.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Smaller craft: Two US officials told CBS News Iran could use smaller boats to lay mines in the strait, which would make them harder to spot and stop.</li><li>Oil route risk: Explainers noted the strait’s narrow geography makes mining especially dangerous: even a small number of explosives can push ships into limited channels and drive up insurance and shipping costs.</li><li>Ground-war warning: Al-Monitor reported a US senator warning that the conflict’s trajectory could pull the United States closer to a ground war.</li><li>Deleted-escort post: The Straits Times reported the US energy secretary deleted a post about the Navy escorting a vessel through the Strait of Hormuz—an episode other coverage linked to broader uncertainty about what’s happening in the shipping lane.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US government (President Trump): President Trump said he had no reports that Iran had started, or was about to start, mining the Strait of Hormuz. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-iranian-mine-laying-vessels-destroyed-near-strait-of-hormuz-trump-warning/article70728419.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>US intelligence sources: US intelligence reporting cited by multiple outlets said Iran had begun laying mines, or was signaling it may deploy them, in the Strait of Hormuz. (<a href='https://edition.cnn.com/2026/03/10/politics/iran-begins-laying-mines-in-strait-of-hormuz'>CNN</a>)</li><li>Iranian leadership (state stance): Iran said it would block regional oil exports, according to US and regional coverage. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-us-military-says-it-destroyed-16-iranian-mine-laying-boats-near-strait-of-hormuz-amid-trumps-warning-11197751#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>US lawmakers (cautionary view): A US senator warned that escalating actions could push the US closer to a ground war, and urged closer attention to the risks of further expansion. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/trump-warns-iran-over-hormuz-mines-senator-cautions-us-may-be-nearing-ground-war'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/03/11/us-steps-up-strikes-on-iran-destroys-16-mine-laying-vessels-and-raises-pressure-in-hormuz'>US steps up strikes on Iran, destroys 16 mine-laying vessels and raises pressure in Hormuz</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-iranian-mine-laying-vessels-destroyed-near-strait-of-hormuz-trump-warning/article70728419.ece'>U.S. military destroys at least 16 Iranian mine-laying vessels ‘near Strait of Hormuz’</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/us-energy-secretary-deletes-post-about-navy-escorting-vessel-through-st